From a5681d4877a9bf286073aa4788a9386382d0b946 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LightCraft additional extensions <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:26:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] Export: After export can show the files or open them in
 an application

The Export dialog gets an After export choice, like Lightroom Classic's
Post-Processing > After Export: Do nothing, Show in Finder / Explorer / the
file manager, Open in PhotoCraft, or Open in Other Application... (an app
name for `open -a` on macOS, a program path elsewhere; typed or picked with
Choose...). It is an export option (`afterExport`: "nothing" |
"showInFileManager" | "openInPhotoCraft" | {"openIn": app}), so export
presets, Export with Previous and `app.export` params carry it; an unknown
value is refused before anything is written.

The desktop app does it on the UI thread once the export has finished and
wrote files (export_task poll, or before a foreground `app.export`
answers), not after a cancel. PhotoCraft is found as Photo > Edit In finds
it. A failure becomes a note on the export toast, never a panic. Where the
host has no file manager or launcher (MCP, lightcraft-cli, tests, the web)
the files are written and the result reports the action as skipped.
`dialog.exportChooseApp {app?}` sets the application of the open dialog.

Adapted from upstream PR #3649 (closed unmerged) to v0.20.0. Simplified and
Traditional Chinese translations for the new strings; tests in
tests/after_export.rs (dialog, Export with Previous, presets, the action
after export with fake services), engine and MCP tests.

